message.content:
I enhanced and zoomed the tooth-bearing regions and graded what I could see. These are reads from a single panoramic image, so a periapical radiograph or a clinical exam should confirm them.

```json
{"lesions": [
  {"box": [0.338, 0.611, 0.378, 0.677], "pai": 3},
  {"box": [0.636, 0.611, 0.671, 0.681], "pai": 3}
]}
```

1. **Lower right first molar (image left):** an area of mineral loss at the apex and between the roots, with blurred trabecular bone and no sharp border. I'm fairly confident in this one.
2. **Lower left molar under the bridge (image right):** some radiolucency around the apices of the abutment roots. This is the less certain call, because the metal bridge and overlapping structures make it hard to judge.

I found no definite periapical radiolucencies in the upper jaw or the front teeth.
